From ba8e13b794130613cd124a94a94922bb73738586 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Bestmann <oliver.bestmann@googlemail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Mar 2026 19:26:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] backends/native: Move cursor to overlay plane.

Overlay planes on apple hardware can not be exposed as cursor planes
due to them having some limitations. Because of that, mutter is not
able to take advantage of those planes to enable hardware compositing
for the cursor. The most relevant restriction is that at least 32x32px
of the overlay must be visible on the screen, otherwise the dcp crashes.

This hack makes the drm overlay planes available as cursor planes. It
then adds transparent padding to the cursor, so that the intersection between
cursor and screen has always at least the required size.

Signed-off-by: Oliver Bestmann <oliver.bestmann@googlemail.com>
